      "writtenOn": "2021-05-24T02:49:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea is just to run a workload with and without this change and look at the kernel memory allocated (dumpsys memory or cat /proc/meminfo). I would be fine with doing this experiment with some common mobile workloads (eg,chrome with several tabs, or a camera workload).\n\nIt may be that adding an element to rwlock and mutex makes no difference at all. We\u0027d like to confirm that before taking this change.",
